WEBVTT

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.410
Riru...

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.060
It's been a while, Suzuko.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.360
You have been chosen

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.030
to be a Selector.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:55.720
After talking with Kiyoi-chan and the 
others, I thought it might happen, but...

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.380
A new Selector battle has begun.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.180
It's already started.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.360
It was finally over, 
after everyone suffered so much...

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.020
I can't go through that again!

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.950
I'm sorry, Suzuko.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.310
I didn't want to come here.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.150
I knew that if I met you, 
I would make you suffer again.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.280
So the rules are the same this time, then.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.490
Battles where you fight 
someone for their memories.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.510
I don't know the details myself.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.200
What I do know is that everyone 
starts with three coins,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.440
and if you win, you can 
alter memories to your liking.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.540
There's a new element called a "key card,"

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.420
and if you lose, your LRIG is taken.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.310
Alter memories?

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.240
Huh? Yeah...

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.140
Erase memories, or bring them back.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.980
Erase or bring back memories...

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.900
Does it have to be my own memories?

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.860
Can I recover someone else's memories?

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.390
I haven't been told anything about 
what memories can be changed.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.300
It might be possible.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.920
If I could get back someone else's memories...

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:12.970
Suzuko...

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:16.250
I might be able to get 
Chi-chan's memories back.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.860
Chi-chan...

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.380
You're right. There is a possibility.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.520
If you can take back memories by winning,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.940
that means the stolen memories 
must be kept somewhere.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.730
All the lost memories must be somewhere...

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.780
Chi-chan's memories...

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.260
All those important memories we shared...

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.130
But, Suzuko, this is all just my guess.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.540
There's no guarantee.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:58.600
If you don't participate, you can keep 
your peaceful, ordinary life.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.050
That may be what's best for you.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.010
You really are nice, Riru.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.440
But if there's any chance, 
no matter how small,

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.320
I want to bet on it.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.420
If I can get Chi-chan's memories back...

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:20.800
Suzuko...

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:23.860
Okay.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.700
Let's fight together again.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.500
Yeah!

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.260
<i>She's wonderful, that girl.</i>

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.010
<i>Mizushima Kiyoi...</i>

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.170
I won't let you have your way.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:49.000
This time, I will put a stop 
to these Selector battles

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.810
and this endless cycle of despair!

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.270
<i>Another Selector was chosen 
this evening, then?</i>

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.040
<i>I won't let it end.</i>

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.690
<i>There's no escaping this eternal cycle...</i>

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.530
Why?

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.110
Explain it to me, Hanayo-san!

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.500
Why did I become a Selector again?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.320
First Hitoe, then me?

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.310
Then, is Ruuko also...

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:18.630
I don't know.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.460
But even now, more and more 
Selectors are being chosen.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.470
The battles have already begun.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.180
I think I feel a little better 
after talking to Yuzuki.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:36.690
Looks like you're getting along 
well with Yuzuki and Ruuko.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:37.890
Yeah!

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:42.520
The three of us just entered a 
WIXOSS tournament as a team!

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:45.920
Ruuko and I are trying to play carefully,

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.610
but Yuzuki keeps pushing harder and harder.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.960
Afterward, we all meet up to 
discuss how we can improve.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:54.520
I'm happy for you, Hitoe.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:57.490
I've finally found you.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.450
I'm Layla.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.810
I was chosen to be a Selector,

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.230
but I couldn't find anyone to play with.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.720
I was starting to get really frustrated.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.930
So come on! Give me a quickie!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.140
I'm rock hard and ready to go!

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:14.600
Hitoe...

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:27.150
I once fought a Selector like you.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.910
She was self-centered, and aggressive...

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.490
She didn't care about other people.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.960
She would abuse the people 
around her to satisfy her lust...

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.750
You smell just like her.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.180
It smells rotten, like a drainage ditch, right?

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.220
So what?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.680
All I care about is being 
able to do a Selector battle!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.860
Will you fight or won't you? Which is it?

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.390
Hitoe, there's no reason 
to accept her challenge.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.320
Let's run.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:13.260
I don't want to get involved in 
a battle with memories at stake.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:17.120
There are many memories I don't want to 
forget, memories I don't want to lose...

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:22.710
But that's exactly why I can't let 
people like you have your way!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.730
If I don't stop you here, people will suffer!

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:27.590
Hitoe...

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.940
Oh? Looks like you're more than 
just a gloomy girl in glasses.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.010
This'll be fun.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:36.390
Open.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:55.540
Hitoe, I didn't think you'd 
agree to this battle.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:56.620
Neither did I.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:00.700
I'm actually so scared, I'm shaking.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.630
So, Midoriko...

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.710
Will you fight with me?

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.290
Of course.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:08.660
Grow!

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.530
Huh? That girl...

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.730
She has no LRIG. What's going on?

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:16.670
Here I go.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:17.470
Unlock.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.970
Coin bet.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:23.230
What?

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.400
This body is so much nicer than my other one.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.230
I feel alive.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.740
Wh-What happened?

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.710
The Selector herself became an LRIG?

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.000
Why?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.640
If you do that, you'll suffer all 
the LRIG's damage yourself.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.370
You'll be badly hurt!

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.530
That's great, isn't it?

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:52.090
I only feel alive when I 
expose myself to danger!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.340
This is the real battle 
I've been looking for!

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.960
She's betting not just 
her coins, but herself?

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.310
That's... That's crazy!

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:05.330
Yeah, I'm crazy! I went 
crazy a long time ago!

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.150
Midoriko!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.440
It's no fun fighting if you won't hit back!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.900
Entertain me more!

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.100
Hitoe, calm down.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:18.160
Don't get sucked into her pace.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.370
Thank you, Midoriko.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.290
I'm okay.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.490
Just a little scared.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.040
Alraune, Kyuuso.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.670
Okay.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:37.810
Nice!

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.010
That was great!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:46.600
Get Wave!

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.360
That was close.

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.820
Hitoe, you've gotten stronger.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:01.830
It's because everyone was there for me. 
Ruuko and Yuzuki, and Midoriko...

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.430
You're not bad.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:08.060
Let's see you go a little harder!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:08.920
Grow!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.940
Hitoe, let's use our coin, too!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:15.460
Yeah!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.800
Coin bet!

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.050
Tentacle!

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.060
Now!

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.140
We won't lose.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.990
Hitoe and I will keep winning to the end.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:01.290
This is the stuff!

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:07.220
Thrills and terror that rip at your flesh, 
burn your bones, and grab your heart...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.350
This is the battle I wanted!

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.310
What is she saying?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:14.440
Here I go!

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.070
Coin bet!

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.740
Doping.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.660
She used a coin to buff herself.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:33.130
Hitoe, build up Ener and 
let's use a gamma burst!

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.220
It's the only way to win!

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:36.000
Yeah.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.260
In High Spirits!

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:46.180
Okay, we'll defend, and on our next turn...

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:51.890
Not yet! Not yet! Not yet! Not yet!

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:54.420
What are you doing?

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.150
Your attacks can't hurt me.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:01.450
And your enhanced attack 
power is hurting you!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.610
So... why?

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.120
This is great! I can't get enough!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.980
This is the joy of living!

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:10.830
Ride!

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.860
I've never seen an LRIG like this...

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.900
She's completely different from us.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:20.760
Insanity... Ecstasy... No, chaos!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.010
This isn't...

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:38.480
Hitoe...

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:41.620
Midoriko! No!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:43.780
Wait!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.550
Midoriko, don't go!

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.650
Not yet...

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:01.900
I'm not satisfied yet.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:05.590
I want more Selector battles 
where I risk everything.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.420
Midori-san...

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.940
Confirmation.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:21.570
Kiyoi-san sent us information 
about the new Selector battles.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.570
Did you learn something?

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.720
Of course.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.990
This time, if you lose, 
your opponent takes your LRIG.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.000
Oh, my!

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.490
So if you lose deliberately,

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:39.090
I'll be taken by some strange Selector and 
spend the rest of my life as their plaything!

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:42.170
Anger. An LRIG is the core of a deck.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.640
I would never be so foolish 
as to let someone take mine.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.910
Oh, dear. What a shame.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:49.300
Hmm?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.800
What's wrong?

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.890
A Selector is approaching.

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.560
Satomi Kou...

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:02.030
No, Carnival.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:06.780
I'm happy to see you again, Mikage Hanna.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.120
Coincidence.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.200
I was thinking the same thing.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.950
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.430
Oh?

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:18.820
Question. Why are you participating 
in these battles again?

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:22.750
You were an LRIG. Are there 
memories you want back?

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:26.280
Memories are chains that bind you.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:30.680
These chains stop people from going forward.

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:34.060
I've seen far too many Selectors like that.

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:39.220
Selectors whose lives are ruled by 
their memories, and who suffer for it.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:43.270
The joy and powerful stimulation of 
being able to see that up close...

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.400
That's what Kou and I wanted.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.360
Anger. We're not here for your entertainment.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.990
And...

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:54.830
Memories can drive people forward, too.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.790
This won't go the way you're hoping it will.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:00.820
Kou failed.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.500
But, Mikage Hanna,

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.880
I can get along with you just fine.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.710
The same with that other girl, Homura Suzuko.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.920
I'm sure the look on her face when she 
sinks into despair will be exquisite!

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:16.400
I'm overjoyed that I'll get a 
chance to face her so her soon!

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.720
Revenge?!

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.230
Suzuko-san isn't a Selector!

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:22.980
I see. You didn't know yet.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.110
What do you mean?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.990
I'm a little better informed than you.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.700
That's all.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.360
Don't tell me you...

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.160
Obstruction!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.140
Suzuko refuses to delve into this world!

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:38.700
I won't let you touch her!

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:43.240
Open!

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.560
Um... I'm s-sorry!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.060
Don't apologize when you 
haven't done anything.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.850
I've told you again and again.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.000
I'm s-sorry!

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.540
We're going first.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.270
Let's go.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:09.860
Deploying two tricks.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.820
That's their LRIG, huh?

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.290
Understanding.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:17.280
That deck is built around 
deck manipulation tactics.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.370
H-How did you know?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.160
Why did you tell her?

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.560
Th-That was a lie!

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:25.060
I was just making it up!

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:25.830
Um...

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.570
So she knows my combos, huh?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.040
Attack!

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:34.760
Right! Here I go!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.640
Shut up!

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:41.020
I-I'm sorry.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:44.500
Hanna-sama, did you notice?

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.190
Naturally.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.860
Her reactions are too slow.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.360
She's probably waiting 
for a chance to counter.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.940
That's my Hanna-sama!

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:55.200
Carnival, I'm putting a stop to your plans.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.540
Coin bet!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.620
Blind.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.010
What is this?

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:05.350
Blind, of course.

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:08.320
But it won't be enough to stop me.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.500
Mikage Hanna, I'll show you something nice.

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:14.470
Unlock. Coin bet.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.320
I'm back!

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:24.390
It's everybody's little sister, Aya!

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.250
A second LRIG?

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.860
This is the effect of the key card.

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:31.440
Yay! Yay!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:35.230
Hey, why do I have to support Slow-ko here?

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:37.400
It's normally the other way around, right?

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.880
I-I'm sorry!

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.370
Enough talking.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.560
Coin bet.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.410
Don't screw this up.

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:47.710
Holograph!

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.720
I'm sorry!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:55.380
Magical WIXOSS! It's me, Slow-ko!

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:57.610
I'm sorry!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.050
Screw the Blind effect!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.130
Just keep hitting her!

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:02.860
'Kay!

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.650
I'm sorry!

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.410
Where is Hitoe?

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.980
She's not answering her phone.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.160
Hitoe!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.300
Hitoe, I was so worried!

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.500
Yuzuki!

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:39.590
I couldn't protect Midoriko... Midori-san.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:43.410
If you lose, they take your LRIG?

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:45.540
What the hell kind of rule is that?

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:49.780
These Selector battles are totally 
different from the ones before.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:53.820
You and Ruuko have to stay 
out of it, no matter what!

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.700
I'd have loved to, but...

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:00.230
Hanayo-san!

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:02.720
So you're a Selector, too?

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:03.580
Yeah.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:08.660
If we can't avoid these battles, 
then let's work together to win.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.370
I'll get back Midoriko!

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.290
Yuzuki...

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:17.880
<i>I need to do something, for Hitoe's sake, too.</i>

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.310
I warned you via text.

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:22.490
Awareness.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:28.060
But when I saw that message, I thought 
that now was the time for battling.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:31.400
Unless I have coins to spare,

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.770
I can't fight battles to figure out 
the rules or how my enemies think.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.520
You're crazy.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:40.100
But I didn't intend to lose,

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:42.860
so I feel bad for Anonymous-chan.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.540
I'm glad you're okay, though.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:50.290
Even though you lost your LRIG, 
you still remain a Selector, right?

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:53.110
I still have coins.

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:58.250
But I don't know how to 
fight without an LRIG.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:01.920
We both learned some things 
after we fought battles.

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.400
If you lose, your LRIG is taken.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.740
With the key cards, you can use two LRIGs.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:11.730
Even if you lose, you remain a Selector.

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:14.550
And Carnival's goal...

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:16.980
What she said was probably true.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:21.250
But I think that's only part of it.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:24.700
She has a goal beyond personal pleasure?

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:28.550
Hypothesis. Carnival is 
still hiding something.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:29.160
And...

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.080
I see. You didn't know yet.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.640
I'm a little better informed than you.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.090
That's all.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.330
Certainty.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:42.680
Carnival is deeply involved with the 
heart of these Selector battles.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.990
Things are clearly different than before.

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.850
There's still so much we don't know.

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.250
Agreement.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.820
We'll need to investigate further.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:55.730
Addition. There's one more thing I've learned...

00:20:56.580 --> 00:21:00.990
I was curious about what Carnival 
said, so I called Suzuko-san.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.080
And she said...

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.180
It really is fantastic...

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:21.590
That's right.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:26.240
Continue enjoying the battles any way you want.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.360
I brought more.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.530
What's wrong, Tama?

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:41.890
I hear a voice...

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:47.360
I don't hear anything.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.960
Crowding / Loser and Winner

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.120
I'm getting back Chi-chan's memories.

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:30.280
You may be able to pay the price to get one.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:33.700
So it'll be better to work in a group.

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:35.970
How much of this had you predicted?

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.230
I saw Morikawa Chinatsu...

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:40.980
Gathering / Vortex and Turbid Water

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:40.980
Gathering / Vortex and Turbid Water.
